the regular is perfectly fine. But yeah, the difference in paper quality is pretty noticeable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:23:32-08:00","id":371058,"title":"","content":"For picking up a corebook with illustrations in full color like Requiem 2nd (I assume, as I just checked and Masquerade 2nd doesn't appear to be PoD yet), I'd go the extra mile for premium. I've gotten both premium and standard quality books. Standard works fine if you're on a budget, but the paper is slightly thinner and there is a visible print grain to the illustrations. Premium color isn't quite up to the glossy sturdiness of traditional print full-color books, but it's smoother and a little thicker, the color is a little more vivid, and I'd be a lot more comfortable with premium for a book I would be handling often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 01-15-2015, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:52:36-08:00","id":371091,"title":"","content":"I purchased one book with the standard color, rather than premium. It's a fine book, it does everything the book needs to do, there's no flaws or anything. The paper feels thinner, not as stiff as the premium or pre-POD pages were. The cost can make a huge difference at times, but the result is going to be the same book with the same rules. If you prefer the more usual rpg paper and have money to spend, go for premium, but if you look at pictures once and never again or just use the book for reference material you're probably better off with the standard print.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T09:17:54-08:00","id":371107,"title":"","content":"thanks everyone...went premium","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4636-jarazix","name":"Jarazix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T11:03:37-08:00","id":379217,"title":"","content":"Don't have standard to compare it to...but premium is very nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4636-jarazix","name":"Jarazix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}